course: dictionary
lesson: 8442
title: Safe and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Safe» has several meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. «Your dose depends on your age and weight, which is why someone else's tablets are never safe for you.» Here safe means not likely to cause harm. The clue is the warning: someone else's tablets could hurt you, so they are not safe for you.
explain: Safe can also describe a person, animal or place that is not in danger. «Slow blinks mean a cat feels safe with you.» The cat is relaxed because it is not frightened. «For the same distance, flying on a big airline is much safer than going by car.» Safer is the comparison form, meaning less risk.
explain: Safe can also be a noun. A safe is a strong metal box with a lock, used to keep money and valuables. Same spelling, different job: ask yourself whether safe is describing something or naming a thing. When in doubt, swap in another word and see if the sentence still works.
fact: «Safe» means not in danger, and not likely to be hurt.
fact: «Safe» can also mean not likely to cause harm, as in «safe to eat» or «a safe place».
fact: «Safe» can mean careful and not taking risks, as in «a safe driver».
fact: A safe is also a strong metal box with a lock, for money and valuables.
fact: Useful phrases: «safe and sound», «play it safe», and «to be on the safe side».
exercise: «Your dose depends on your age and weight, so someone else's tablets are never safe for you.» In this sentence, safe means | Full of sweets | *Not likely to cause harm to you | A strong metal box with a lock | Very fast and quick
exercise: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops, which give them shade, a lookout and safe dens for cubs.» What does safe mean in «safe dens for cubs»? | Dens made of metal | Dens that are empty and cold | Dens that are very loud | *Places where the cubs are not in danger
exercise: Ben says, «Lock the money in the safe.» What is a safe here? | A word that means careful | A kind of bird | A bus stop | *A strong metal box with a lock
test: «For the same distance, flying on a big airline is much safer than going by car.» Safer means | More dangerous | Louder and busier | Slower and noisier | *Less risky
test: Which phrase means being careful and not taking risks? | safe and sound, to be found | a safe box | *play it safe | safe dens for cubs
exam: After the storm, the children came home. What does «safe and sound» mean? | Lost forever in the storm | Wet through from the rain | Very loud and noisy | *Not hurt and unharmed
